ry conflicts among many African nations after independence', TRUE, 0),('5f07cbe1-51d7-4c04-8186-28c239af1aea'::uuid, '374b0548-8f38-4741-81da-d8f7183f7521'::uuid, 'A single African government', FALSE, 1),('4629aa06-5449-4624-8256-437c3a2b46f8'::uuid, '374b0548-8f38-4741-81da-d8f7183f7521'::uuid, 'An end to all ethnic differences', FALSE, 2),('7e38b142-7f24-4ee1-8c07-d8a97e83d3b1'::uuid, '374b0548-8f38-4741-81da-d8f7183f7521'::uuid, 'Permanent indigenous administrations', FALSE, 3),('0d2bb0c9-0129-4497-84a7-996fa998421b'::uuid, 'acb986c9-364b-4adf-8869-cbb07b1e0a56'::uuid, 'True', TRUE, 0),('23131b52-d239-40cf-8524-f5df589484d9'::uuid, 'acb986c9-364b-4adf-8869-cbb07b1e0a56'::uuid, 'False', FALSE, 1),('97579b97-9c47-4424-873c-ae7b804b5737'::uuid, 'e615efff-a653-4098-837e-8e9067540668'::uuid, 'True', TRUE, 0),('f83b36ea-b8c4-4461-8443-da268799b61f'::uuid, 'e615efff-a653-4098-837e-8e9067540668'::uuid, 'False', FALSE, 1),('34ab061b-4c17-476e-8bad-1dfd4c63564b'::uuid, '2a2f9c17-e502-4e66-8ce9-9b8ffd39235b'::uuid, 'True', FALSE, 0),('c7b77f54-3a09-4d82-8cb7-bf53abe2d7ea'::uuid, '2a2f9c17-e502-4e66-8ce9-9b8ffd39235b'::uuid, 'False', TRUE, 1),('f70ef2c6-91f1-406b-8e6c-145e7c48a1c6'::uuid, 'c7ecb499-8e68-4cd8-8350-308e5632e70a'::uuid, 'True', FALSE, 0),('3cc7a4a0-e731-439b-8eaa-43786d2f0a58'::uuid, 'c7ecb499-8e68-4cd8-8350-308e5632e70a'::uuid, 'False', TRUE, 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET question_id = EXCLUDED.question_id, choice_text = EXCLUDED.choice_text, is_correct = EXCLUDED.is_correct, order_index = EXCLUDED.order_index;
INSERT INTO public.quizzes (id, subject, unit, title, description) VALUES ('c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'History', 'Unit 3', 'Molarum Grade 10 — History Unit 3: Social, Economic and Political Developments in Ethiopia from mid-19th Century to 1941', 'Source-grounded Molarum Grade 10 History questions for Unit 3: Social, Economic and Political Developments in Ethiopia from mid-19th Century to 1941.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET subject = EXCLUDED.subject, unit = EXCLUDED.unit, title = EXCLUDED.title, description = EXCLUDED.description;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, quiz_id, question_type, question_text, correct_answer, explanation, order_index) VALUES ('d2ff99cf-2716-46c7-8093-6050063089e3'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which kingdom''s capital was the starting point for two major nineteenth-century Ethiopian trade routes?', 'Kafa', 'The source says the two major routes started from Bonga, the capital of Kafa Kingdom.', 0),('2c52237c-650d-4eb7-89a1-342592853220'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What served as a medium of exchange alongside Maria Theresa Thalers?', 'Salt bars (amole)', 'The textbook says salt bars, called amole, were used alongside Maria Theresa Thalers.', 1),('2390be35-41ac-4000-811e-e33adc32ce30'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which group was described as the most dominant long-distance traders from the interior to the coast?', 'Muslim merchants', 'The source identifies Muslim merchants as the dominant travelling group.', 2),('abac2132-cc8b-4880-86d8-af110c9554d4'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which activity is listed as a common Ethiopian cottage industry?', 'Metalworking', 'Metalworking is among the cottage industries listed by the textbook.', 3),('678bf9e5-d271-45e0-8928-403cead592cd'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which items were blacksmiths responsible for making?', 'Ploughshares and spearheads', 'The textbook lists agricultural implements and weapons including ploughshares and spearheads.', 4),('d05ddffd-0e3d-477e-8e12-23fb827d00c5'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What throne name did Kassa Hailu take after his 1855 coronation?', 'Tewodros II', 'Kassa Hailu was anointed and became Tewodros II in 1855.', 5),('df804097-39c9-4793-8c4d-c5c795f306c7'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which battle symbolized the end of the Zemene Mesafint?', 'Ayshal', 'The source says Kassa''s defeat of the last Yejju ruler at Ayshal symbolized the end of Zemene Mesafint.', 6),('e307f0ab-258a-40ce-8dea-8b9de4d209e7'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Where did Tewodros establish an arms manufacture with European assistance?', 'Gafat', 'Tewodros established arms manufacture at Gafat near Debre Tabor.', 7),('cd65c45c-3d05-411c-8aee-e12bc404a085'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which ruler did Yohannes IV recognize as Nigus of Shewa under the Liche agreement?', 'Menilek', 'The Liche agreement recognized Menilek as Nigus of Shewa.', 8),('49a73064-6240-46cc-8970-69536abcaea6'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What caused the Great Famine or Kefu Qan according to the textbook?', 'Rinderpest from infected cattle imported through Massawa', 'The source identifies rinderpest triggered by infected cattle imported through Massawa as the immediate cause.', 9),('7a8e3268-051c-4ae2-8d49-7f1784439f48'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What was the first modern bank founded by Menilek II called?', 'Bank of Abyssinia', 'The textbook calls the Bank of Abyssinia the first modern bank, founded by Menilek II.', 10),('5da55b82-5d19-4da8-8a80-e2037ca869ce'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Who commanded the late-1867 British military expedition to Ethiopia?', 'Sir Robert Napier', 'The British expedition was commanded by Sir Robert Napier.', 11),('bcddc0b0-7541-46a2-8476-46569dd22d77'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'At which battle did Yohannes IV and Ras Alula severely defeat Egyptian forces in 1875?', 'Gundat', 'The source identifies Gundat as the 1875 Ethiopian victory over Egyptian troops.', 12),('6eae48b7-e959-4199-8e9d-8ffff58e9e66'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which Ethiopian general defeated Italians at Dogali?', 'Ras Alula Engida', 'The source says Ras Alula Engida defeated Italians at Dogali.', 13),('ffb08a70-6f9b-4231-8fab-4453603e5eb2'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What did Ethiopia agree to facilitate under the Hewett Treaty?', 'Evacuation of Egyptian soldiers from eastern Sudan', 'Ethiopia agreed to facilitate evacuation of Egyptian soldiers in return for use of Massawa among other terms.', 14),('db49aac4-711b-4f29-8db2-eeb12aa44640'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Why did Menilek II abrogate the Treaty of Wuchale?', 'The Italian and Amharic versions differed on Article XVII', 'Crucial differences between the Italian and Amharic versions created misunderstanding; Menilek abrogated it after revision failed.', 15),('ee6c9d89-a412-4223-8347-60c30672d2ee'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which leader is associated with the siege strategy at Mekelle?', 'Empress Taytu', 'The source says the siege of Mekelle was believed to be designed by Empress Taytu.', 16),('7b3624d3-4366-46cc-8bcc-decb887c9f7e'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What did Italy recognize in the Treaty of Addis Ababa after Adwa?', 'Ethiopia''s independence', 'Italy recognized Ethiopia''s independence in the 1896 Treaty of Addis Ababa.', 17),('d47c9a25-d821-4b01-85d7-286494c051e7'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What name did the textbook give to the dual governance beginning in 1916?', 'Diarchy', 'The political settlement after the 1916 revolt began a period of dual governance called diarchy.', 18),('7e2b2bb3-68c4-4323-811a-ac81abfcd9c4'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What name did Ethiopian resistance fighters use during Italian occupation?', 'Patriots (Arbegnoch)', 'The textbook names the Ethiopian resistance fighters Patriots, locally Arbegnoch.', 19),('bb8755a8-0ed2-40df-8d4c-1ac6df2d5bcd'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'true_false', 'Tewodros II tried to replace regional armies with a salaried national army.', 'True', 'The source states that Tewodros tried to organize a salaried national army in place of regional armies.', 20),('93595aae-2bcc-4bfd-8ec8-6516183daa83'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'true_false', 'The Amharic version of Article XVII made use of Italian good offices obligatory.', 'False', 'The Amharic version said Ethiopia could use Italian good offices, while the Italian text made it obligatory.', 21),('3f5942e1-d40c-4f28-8b16-1b1ec616b743'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'true_false', 'The League of Nations was one reason Ethiopia delayed its counter-offensive in 1935.', 'True', 'The text says Ethiopia trusted the League of Nations and international justice, contributing to delay.', 22),('728d99a9-b2aa-4d8a-8d3c-f28c9cc02242'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'true_false', 'Yewust Arbegnoch lived only outside towns and never worked among Italians.', 'False', 'Yewust Arbegnoch lived in towns among Italians and secretly passed vital information to patriots.', 23),('9cf80350-6dc6-44ec-89aa-44ab5d75cc99'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Name one commodity that dominated nineteenth-century Ethiopian long-distance trade.', 'Ivory, civet musk, salt bars, or slaves.', 'The textbook lists these as principal trade commodities.', 24),('75599470-0e97-4e28-82be-75ca11fb9b4d'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Give one internal group that opposed Tewodros''s reforms.', 'Regionalist forces or the clergy.', 'The text identifies regionalist forces and clergy as opponents of his reforms.', 25),('16b92e0b-8cb3-4681-8615-7ab2bb130396'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'State one modern service or technology introduced by Menilek II.', 'The Bank of Abyssinia, a modern school, postal system, railway work, electricity, telephone, telegraph, motor car, plumbing, or coin minting.', 'The source lists these modernization measures.', 26),('ae61ca0a-c5f2-4579-804c-679107b10d3f'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Why did Egyptian leaders seek to occupy northeast Africa including Ethiopia?', 'They wanted to control the source of the Nile.', 'The textbook identifies control of the Nile source as the Egyptian ambition.', 27),('f62a12a3-38e9-4a6b-816b-7c8521e63f2f'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Name one result of the Battle of Adwa for Ethiopia.', 'International recognition of Ethiopia as an independent sovereign state, stronger national integration, or a symbol of unity and national pride.', 'The source lists these results of the victory.', 28),('227545dd-3d81-4eda-8001-3eeec9965196'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Give one power recognized for the emperor by the 1931 Constitution.', 'Appointing or dismissing officials, administering justice, declaring or ending wars, or granting lands and honours.', 'The source identifies these unrestricted imperial rights.', 29),('cdbc9e06-112d-4ba3-825a-b8694887db7a'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Give one reason Italians succeeded in 1936 according to the textbook.', 'Greater preparation, superior weapons, airpower, mustard gas, or Ethiopian logistical problems.', 'The source attributes Italian success to these military advantages and Ethiopian constraints.', 30),('005edc23-83a6-43e1-80d9-69d759f918c1'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'What support did Ethiopian peasants give patriotic resistance fighters?', 'Food, shelter, information, and sometimes direct fighting support.', 'The source says peasantry provided food, shelter, information, and at times fought with patriots.', 31),('44dca079-6128-4eeb-8545-f58091a21a94'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'In what year was Kassa Hailu anointed as Tewodros II?', '1855', 'Kassa Hailu became Tewodros II on 9 February 1855.', 32),('81c8d764-2eeb-4209-89d5-8f401a7786ef'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'How many cannons were produced at Gafat according to the textbook?', '35', 'The source says about 35 cannons were produced at Gafat.', 33),('d0fd0384-4e05-43f4-8a6f-c996a7ebfc48'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'In what year did Tewodros II die at Maqdala after the British expedition?', '1868', 'The source dates Tewodros''s death at Maqdala to 13 April 1868.', 34),('524e424b-60dc-4f9e-8987-5824b3b2effa'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'In what year did Menilek II abrogate the Treaty of Wuchale?', '1893', 'Menilek unilaterally abrogated the treaty in 1893.', 35),('1770722b-8a6d-436b-86b7-b8aefe7965e8'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'In what year was the decisive Battle of Adwa fought?', '1896', 'The decisive Battle of Adwa was fought on 1 March 1896.', 36),('eb2eab76-fabe-48e9-8d48-cc40c0f161d7'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'In what year was Lij Iyasu deposed and Zewditu crowned empress?', '1916', 'The source dates Lij Iyasu''s deposition and Zewditu''s crowning to 1916.', 37),('5cb30660-932c-4357-8f0a-2b69ca66a8be'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'In what year did Italian troops cross the Marab River in the Fascist invasion?', '1935', 'The source dates the Italian crossing of the Marab River to 3 October 1935.', 38),('299204eb-5333-41ff-860e-718274b08d01'::uuid, 'c19a6124-6f3b-4710-8ee0-423ee4bfeac7'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'In what year did Emperor Haile Selassie re-enter Addis Ababa and hoist the Ethiopian flag?', '1941', 'The source says he re-entered the capital and officially hoisted the flag on 5 May 1941.', 39) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET quiz_id = EXCLUDED.quiz_id, question_type = EXCLUDED.question_type, question_text = EXCLUDED.question_text, correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, order_index = EXCLUDED.order_index;
